From 836edec0f4e174c55a04c7234b259e850be9a31b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 06:07:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] drm: do not allow a plain frame commit to modeset

`flags = args.seamless ? 0 : DRM_MODE_ATOMIC_ALLOW_MODESET` was written for
mode switches (fb39c8c, "prefer seamless configs, fallback to blocking"). It
granted ALLOW_MODESET to every ordinary frame as a side effect, because
CreateFrameUpdateCommit() only sets seamless when a mode change is staged.
TestComposition() builds its test-only commit from the same args, so
validation carried the flag as well: the kernel answered "OK" for a plan it
could only realise by tearing the pipe down, the planner never fell back, and
the real commit then did exactly that.

On an AMD Phoenix laptop this is the desktop icons vanishing and returning
every time the mouse starts or stops moving. The pointer sprite appearing adds
a layer; hwcomposer tries the cursor plane or an overlay for it; amdgpu DCN
treats the plane-topology change as a full update; with ALLOW_MODESET set it
performs a modeset rather than rejecting, and a modeset blanks the panel for a
frame. The commit succeeds, so nothing is logged. SurfaceFlinger's output is
intact, so screencap shows a perfect desktop. No display reconfiguration is
visible to Android because it all happens inside one atomic commit -- which
is why crash-loop, hotplug, commit-failure, MES, plan-flip, source-crop and
cursor-only-commit theories were all measured and eliminated first.

ALLOW_MODESET is now set only when a modeset is actually requested: a
display_mode, a power_mode, or a teardown. Real modesets keep their previous
behaviour exactly -- blocking ones get the flag, seamless ones try without it
and retry with it. A plain frame the hardware cannot page-flip to now fails its
test-only commit with EINVAL, and the existing fallback chain (cursor fallback
-> all-client) runs before anything reaches the screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NzM9d6UTbgoE8FxzXbB9QK
Change-Id: I267eca69a53f46986f2182a580c2279887d7a0d2
---
 drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
index a462f97..9937017 100644
--- a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
+++ b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
@@ -128,7 +128,40 @@ std::optional<AtomicCommitResult> DrmAtomicStateManager::CommitFrame(
     return std::nullopt;
   }
 
-  uint32_t flags = args.seamless ? 0U : DRM_MODE_ATOMIC_ALLOW_MODESET;
+  // DRM_MODE_ATOMIC_ALLOW_MODESET only when a modeset is actually being asked
+  // for -- a mode change, a power transition, or a teardown.
+  //
+  // The previous form, `seamless ? 0 : ALLOW_MODESET`, was written for mode
+  // switches ("prefer seamless configs, fallback to blocking") and granted the
+  // flag to every PLAIN FRAME as a side effect, because CreateFrameUpdateCommit
+  // only sets seamless when a mode change is staged. And TestComposition builds
+  // its test-only commit from the same args, so validation carried the flag
+  // too: the kernel would answer "OK" for a plan it could only realise by
+  // tearing the pipe down, the planner never fell back, and the real commit
+  // then did exactly that.
+  //
+  // What that looks like: on an AMD Phoenix laptop the desktop icons vanished
+  // and came back every time the mouse started or stopped moving. The pointer
+  // sprite appearing adds a layer; hwcomposer tries the cursor plane (or an
+  // overlay) for it; amdgpu DCN treats that plane-topology change as needing a
+  // full update; with ALLOW_MODESET set it performs a modeset instead of
+  // rejecting -- and a modeset blanks the panel for a frame. The commit
+  // SUCCEEDS, so nothing is logged; SurfaceFlinger's output is intact, so
+  // screencap shows a perfect desktop; no display reconfiguration is visible
+  // to Android because it all happens inside one atomic commit. Seven other
+  // theories were eliminated by measurement before this one was read out of
+  // the code.
+  //
+  // Without the flag, a plan the hardware cannot page-flip to fails its
+  // test-only commit with EINVAL, and the planner's existing fallback chain
+  // (cursor fallback -> all-client) does its job before anything reaches the
+  // screen. Real modesets keep their previous behaviour exactly: blocking ones
+  // get the flag, seamless ones try without it and retry with it below.
+  const bool requests_modeset = args.display_mode.has_value() ||
+                                args.power_mode.has_value() || args.teardown;
+  uint32_t flags = (requests_modeset && !args.seamless)
+                       ? DRM_MODE_ATOMIC_ALLOW_MODESET
+                       : 0U;
   const int error_buf_max_size = 64;
   char err_buf[error_buf_max_size];
   auto *drm = pipe_->device;
